  "caption": "Detective Quinn took on the case of the sore leg: back or hip? The internet only made it worse.\n\nWhere it hurts is a big clue. Nerve-related pain (sciatica) often travels below the knee, sometimes with tingling, and may be worse with sitting. Hip joint pain tends to sit in the groin. Outer-hip pain that's sore at night or on stairs can be a tendon.\n\nWhat often helps: keep moving gently and break up sitting for nerve-type pain, strength work for the hip joint, and less squeeze on a sore outer hip (pillow between the knees). Don't stretch blindly; find the source first.\n\nSaddle numbness, bladder or bowel changes or a weakening leg need urgent care. Not improving in a couple of weeks? Get assessed.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
